sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Admin
    participant Upload as /api/upload
    participant Blob as Azure Blob Storage

    A->>Upload: POST { fileName, contentType, category: "audio" }
    Upload->>Upload: Validate MIME (mp3 / m4a / wav / ogg) via lib/upload.ts
    Upload->>Upload: Check size under MAX_FILE_SIZES.audio
    Upload->>Upload: Generate key "audio/<uuid>/<filename>"
    Upload->>Blob: Generate presigned SAS PUT URL (1hr)
    Blob-->>Upload: SAS URL
    Upload-->>A: { upload_url, key, container }
    A->>Blob: PUT raw audio file directly via SAS URL\n(client → blob, never proxied through Next.js)
    Note over Blob: Object stored in private container.\nNo separate transcoding step today — HLS .m3u8\ncan be uploaded alongside the source if pre-transcoded.

    actor U as Listener
    participant Player as Audio Player
    participant Hook as useHlsPlayer
    participant Media as /api/media (streaming proxy)
    participant Store as Player Store (Zustand)

    U->>Player: Click play on AuditBrief
    Player->>Store: loadAuditBrief({ id, title, audioShortUrl, audioLongUrl, ... })
    Store-->>Hook: currentAuditBrief changed
    Hook->>Hook: Resolve URL via /api/media?key=<encoded blob key>
    alt HLS stream (.m3u8)
        Hook->>Hook: new Hls() → loadSource() → attachMedia()
    else Direct file (mp3 / m4a)
        Hook->>Hook: audio.src = mediaProxyUrl
    end

    Hook->>Media: GET /api/media?key=audio/<uuid>/file.mp3
    Media->>Blob: streamObject(key, range?) via Azure SDK\n  (Node ReadableStream → Web ReadableStream)
    Blob-->>Media: Audio bytes + Content-Range (if range requested)
    Media-->>Hook: 200 OK or 206 Partial Content
    Note over Media: lib/storage.ts streams without buffering;\nsuitable for files up to several GB.

    Hook->>Store: setDuration(...)
    loop Every timeupdate event
        Hook->>Store: setCurrentTime(...)
    end

    U->>Player: Toggle Short / Long audio
    Player->>Store: toggleAudioType()
    Store-->>Hook: audioType changed → new key resolved, source reattached
